   Multiplication by sqrt(2+sqrt(3)) yields sqrt(4-3) = 1.
c) 3-2sqrt(2) = (sqrt(2)-1)^2, sqrt(2)-1 > 0.
   sixthroot(3-2sqrt(2)) = cbrt(sqrt(2)-1).
   Multiplication by cbrt(1+sqrt(2)) yields cbrt(2-1) = 1.
   The principal square root here is sqrt(2)-1, not 1-sqrt(2).
d) 6+4sqrt(2) = (2+sqrt(2))^2.
   fourthroot(6+4sqrt(2)) = sqrt(2+sqrt(2)).
   Product with sqrt(4-2sqrt(2)) is
   sqrt((4-2sqrt(2))*(2+sqrt(2))) = sqrt(4) = 2.
   Both square-root factors have positive radicands.
